      "writtenOn": "2025-08-26T15:27:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t we actually just drop `BindingNotUsed` from the enum? AFAICT, the reason it\u0027s there for the other binding resources is because they are all present in the core `BindGroupEntry` struct, so they need some way to signal that they are not being used for that entry.\n\nBut `TexelBufferBindingEntry`, like `StaticSamplerBindingLayout`, is a chained struct, and so its presence is checked with `.Get\u003c\u003e` instead. So it feels like we don\u0027t need `BindingNotUsed` at all for texel buffers? Otherwise we have an enum value that is never valid, which is odd.",
      "parentUuid": "ac2e6a8f_33e30afd",
      "range": {
